From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:08:46 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Build the EROFS tools with Zstandard

The upstream sources support Zstandard (lib/compressor_libzstd.c and the
decoder in lib/decompress.c), but the Android build leaves the encoder out
and does not define HAVE_LIBZSTD, so mkfs.erofs rejects -zzstd and
fsck.erofs cannot read a Zstandard image. Compile the encoder and define
the feature next to the other compressors.

The static_libs of a static library are not linked into its users, so a
libzstd listed there reaches only the three tools of this project; apex-ls
and update_engine's payload generator, which link liberofs with their own
library lists, failed to link. Make liberofs carry libzstd itself
(whole_static_libs) on the host, the device and in recovery, so every user
of the library links without a change.

AOSP's zstd.h marks ZSTD_getDecompressedSize deprecated, which the
module's -Werror turns into an error in lib/decompress.c. The library's
own switch silences the notice.
---
 Android.bp | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Android.bp b/Android.bp
index 7ca293faae2fef1166c5a0e0383a576af3030a51..3460df7a299cbc207f10533fad0591d405bda54c 100644
--- a/Android.bp
+++ b/Android.bp
@@ -66,6 +66,8 @@ cc_defaults {
         "-DHAVE_LINUX_TYPES_H",
         "-DHAVE_LIBSELINUX",
         "-DHAVE_LIBUUID",
+        "-DHAVE_LIBZSTD",
+        "-DZSTD_DISABLE_DEPRECATE_WARNINGS",
         "-DLZ4_ENABLED",
         "-DLZ4HC_ENABLED",
         "-DWITH_ANDROID",
@@ -132,7 +134,13 @@ cc_library {
     ],
     exclude_srcs: [
         "lib/compressor_libdeflate.c",
-        "lib/compressor_libzstd.c",
+    ],
+    // The static_libs of a static library are not linked into its users, which
+    // list liberofs's other dependencies themselves, so every user of the
+    // library (apex-ls, update_engine's payload generator, the three tools)
+    // would need libzstd too. Carry it in the archive instead.
+    whole_static_libs: [
+        "libzstd",
     ],
     export_include_dirs: ["include"],
 
